gfanInterface -- a Macaulay2 interface to gfan
**********************************************

Description
===========

gfanInterface is an interface to Anders Jensen's Gfan software (available at
http://home.imf.au.dk/jensen/software/gfan/gfan.html), which is a C++ program
to compute the Groebner fan (i.e. all the initial ideals) of an ideal.

The main function in this package is *note gfan: gfan, which computes all of
the Groebner bases and initial ideals of a given ideal.  A useful feature of
this function is that it can handle symmetries in the ideal. If you want the
geometric information of this list of Groebner basis, see *note
gfanGroebnerCone: gfanGroebnerCone,.

Most of the functions in gfanInterface require *note MarkedPolynomialList:
MarkedPolynomialList, marked polynomial lists as input. In a marked polynomial
list, the leading term of each polynomial is distinguished. New users should
read the guide *note Conventions for calling methods with options: Conventions
for calling methods with options,. Since gfan is distributed with Macaulay2,
one rarely needs to consult the guide for *note Installation and Configuration
of gfanInterface: Installation and Configuration of gfanInterface,.

Most of functions in the gfan package are accessible through this interface. If
you wish to use one whose interface is not included here send a message to the
package author. Also, please feel free to suggest changes to the parameter
types and return types of each method.

