polynomial being the first ones listed). Use this option if it takes too much t
starting (standard degree lexicographic) Groebner basis and the input is alread

--symmetry:
 Tells the program to read in generators for a group of symmetries (subgroup of
read in the ideal. The program checks that the ideal stays fixed when permuting
respect to elements in the group. The program uses breadth first search to comp
reduced Groebner bases up to symmetry with respect to the specified subgroup.

-e:
 Echo. Output the generators for the symmetry group.

--disableSymmetryTest:
 When using --symmetry this option will disable the check that the group read o
actually is a symmetry group with respect to the input ideal.

--parameters value:
 With this option you can specify how many variables to treat as parameters ins
This makes it possible to do computations where the coefficient field is the fi
functions in the parameters.
--interrupt value:
 Interrupt the enumeration after a specified number of facets have been compute
symmetric traversals, but may not work in general for non-symmetric traversals 
restricted to fans).
