MPLConverter -- Converts lists or ideals into markedPolynomialLists
*******************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        G = MPLConverter{L}
        G = MPLConverter(I)
  * Inputs:
      * L, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, of polynomials
      * I, an *note ideal: (Macaulay2Doc)Ideal,, contained in a polynomial ring
  * Outputs:
      * G, a *note marked polynomial list: MarkedPolynomialList,, a marked
        polynomial of I

Description
===========

This method converts ideals and lists into marked polynomial lists. The output
is a MarkedPolynomialList. The input can be given as an Ideal or List of
polynomials.



+-------------------------------------------+
|i1 : QQ[x,y];                              |
+-------------------------------------------+
|i2 : I = ideal(x^2 + y^2, x*y + y^2 + y^3);|
|                                           |
|o2 : Ideal of QQ[x..y]                     |
+-------------------------------------------+
|i3 : MPLConverter(I)                       |
|                                           |
|        2     2    3           2           |
|o3 = {(x ) + y , (y ) + x*y + y }          |
|                                           |
|o3 : MarkedPolynomialList                  |
+-------------------------------------------+
+---------------------------------------------+
|i4 : QQ[x,y];                                |
+---------------------------------------------+
|i5 : MPLConverter{x^2 + y^2, x*y + y^2 + y^3}|
|                                             |
|        2     2    3           2             |
|o5 = {(x ) + y , (y ) + x*y + y }            |
|                                             |
|o5 : MarkedPolynomialList                    |
+---------------------------------------------+

Ways to use MPLConverter:
=========================

  * "MPLConverter(Ideal)"
  * "MPLConverter(List)"

For the programmer
==================

The object *note MPLConverter: MPLConverter, is a *note method function with
options: (Macaulay2Doc)MethodFunctionWithOptions,.

